.TH TASK3 1
.SH NAME
task3 \- Process Manager for Task Variant 3
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./os_project
(And choose option 2 from the main menu)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B task3
is a terminal-based Process Manager. It allows the user to inspect running processes, group processes by user, display PIDs, stop and continue processes, and send signals.
.SH MENU
.TP
.B 1
List all processes in the system.
.TP
.B 2
Group processes according to their user.
.TP
.B 3
Display the PIDs of all processes.
.TP
.B 4
Stop or continue a selected process.
.TP
.B 5
Send a selected signal to a process.
.TP
.B 0
Exit the program.
.SH SIGNALS
The program supports common signals including:
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Hang up.
.TP
.B SIGINT
Interrupt.
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Terminate.
.TP
.B SIGSTOP
Stop a process.
.TP
.B SIGCONT
Continue a stopped process.
.TP
.B SIGKILL
Forcefully terminate a process.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the program:
.B ./os_project
and navigate to the Process Manager.
.SH NOTES
Some signals require appropriate permissions. Do not send SIGKILL or SIGSTOP to critical system processes.
.SH AUTHOR
Task Variant 3 Team
